   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax in\nthe town of Skaneateles; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5735",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5735-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-hhh, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5735\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax\nin the town of Skaneateles; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Village of Skaneateles (Onondaga County) to impose a\nhotel/motel occupancy tax up to five percent\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Adds new section 1202-hhh to the tax law, which lays out the\nterms for the Village of Skaneateles to impose a hotel occupancy tax of\nno more than five percent.\n\nSection 2: Adds the effective date and will expire December 31, 2026\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is being introduced at the request of the Village of Skanea-\nteles, in order to provide the village an additional revenue source. A\nsimilar bill to this has been introduced for the Town of Skaneateles,\nwhich carved out the village in order that the village will not be\nsubject to a double five percent tax..\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and be deemed repealed December\n31, 2026.\n",
