    "lawCode": "Add §1202-hhh, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5735A\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax\nin the town of Skaneateles; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Town of Skaneateles (Onondaga County), excluding the\nVillage of Skaneateles, to impose a hotel/motel occupancy tax up to five\npercent\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Adds new section 1202-hhh to the tax law, which lays out the\nterms for the Town of Skaneateles to impose a hotel occupancy tax of no\nmore than five percent.\n\nSection 2: Adds the effective date and will expire December 31, 2025\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is being introduced at the request of the Town of Skaneateles,\nin order to provide the town an additional revenue source. This bill\ncarves out the Village of Skaneateles, which will not be subject to this\noccupancy tax.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and be deemed repealed December\n31, 2025.\n",
